=== G3 MECHANISM (1): backend/Dockerfile:17 `COPY backend/ ./` ===
$ rg -n 'COPY backend/' backend/Dockerfile
17:COPY backend/ ./
# The stage copies the WHOLE backend/ tree into /app (data + prompts included),
# then `pip install -e .` (line 19) points the package at that copied source.

=== G3 MECHANISM (2): .dockerignore `data` + `backend/data` vs backend/app/data ===
$ rg -n 'data' .dockerignore
19:data
20:backend/data
# Docker docs (docs.docker.com/build/building/context): "Leading and trailing
# slashes in ignore patterns are disregarded"; matching uses Go filepath.Match;
# a pattern with no slash matches only that name at the CONTEXT ROOT (the docs'
# `temp?` row: "in the root directory"). So `data` == root /data only, and
# `backend/data` == /backend/data only. Neither matches /backend/app/data.
# No `**/data` or `app/data` pattern exists. -> the vendored taxonomy survives.

